From: chasey-dev <ellenyoung0912@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] cfg80211: use INFO for DFS CAC scan rejection

DFS CAC on a local AP prevents scanning on the same PHY. mt_wifi7 logs
this expected condition at ERROR for every scan request, so APCLI scan
retries produce repeated error messages during CAC.

The message now uses INFO, making it available for diagnosis at a level
appropriate for a temporary scan restriction.

Signed-off-by: chasey-dev <ellenyoung0912@gmail.com>
---
--- a/mt_wifi/os/linux/cfg80211/cfg80211drv.c
+++ b/mt_wifi/os/linux/cfg80211/cfg80211drv.c
@@ -3542,7 +3542,7 @@ static int CFG80211DRV_OpsScan(
 		struct DOT11_H *pDot11h = &pAd->Dot11_H;
 
 		if (pDot11h && (pDot11h->ChannelMode == CHAN_SILENCE_MODE)) {
-			MTWF_DBG(pAd, DBG_CAT_CHN, CATCHN_SCAN, DBG_LVL_ERROR,
+			MTWF_DBG(pAd, DBG_CAT_CHN, CATCHN_SCAN, DBG_LVL_INFO,
 			"still in silence mode, can not trigger scan\n");
 			CFG80211OS_ScanEnd(pAd, TRUE);
 			return -EBUSY;
